From: ZephyrCI <kucingbalap1644@ZephyrCI>
Subject: [PATCH] block: enforce ADIOS 3.3.0 over mq-deadline sysfs requests

MediaTek vendor init scripts (init.mt6878.power.rc / init.mt6878.rc)
explicitly write "mq-deadline" into /sys/block/sd*/queue/scheduler during
on init and on property:sys.boot_completed=1, which would override
CONFIG_MQ_IOSCHED_DEFAULT_ADIOS=y after boot.

When CONFIG_MQ_IOSCHED_DEFAULT_ADIOS is enabled, transparently redirect
sysfs switches targeting "mq-deadline" to "adios" while keeping
CONFIG_MQ_IOSCHED_DEADLINE=y for full KMI/vendor compatibility and
allowing explicit switches to other schedulers (kyber, bfq, none).

---
--- a/block/elevator.c	2026-11-19 05:20:59
+++ b/block/elevator.c	2026-11-19 05:20:59
@@ -767,7 +767,12 @@
 	}
 
 	strlcpy(elevator_name, name, sizeof(elevator_name));
-	e = elevator_get(q, strstrip(elevator_name), true);
+	strstrip(elevator_name);
+#ifdef CONFIG_MQ_IOSCHED_DEFAULT_ADIOS
+	if (!strcmp(elevator_name, "mq-deadline"))
+		strlcpy(elevator_name, "adios", sizeof(elevator_name));
+#endif
+	e = elevator_get(q, elevator_name, true);
 	if (!e)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
